# Privacy Policy for Legend Run

**Last updated: 20 August 2026**

Legend Run ("the app", "we", "us") is developed and published by Steven. This
policy explains what data the app processes, why, and who it is shared with.

## Summary

Legend Run has no user accounts, no login, and no server of our own. Your game
progress never leaves your device. The app does, however, display third-party
advertising and collects anonymous usage analytics, and those services process
some data about your device. The details are below.

## Data stored on your device only

The following is saved locally on your device using the operating system's
standard app storage, and is **never transmitted to us or to anyone else**:

- Your high scores and the Top 10 leaderboard, including any nickname you
  choose to enter
- Your selected visual theme and weather settings
- Sound and performance preferences
- Whether you have seen the tutorial

The in-app leaderboard is a **local leaderboard**. It ranks only the scores
achieved on your own device. There is no global or online leaderboard, and we
operate no server that receives your scores. Deleting the app removes this data
permanently. You can also clear it at any time from the leaderboard screen.

## Advertising

The app displays advertisements supplied by **Google AdMob**. To serve ads,
Google may collect and process:

- Your device's advertising identifier (IDFA on iOS, Advertising ID on Android)
- Device and connection information, such as device model, operating system
  version, language, and coarse location derived from IP address
- Information about your interaction with advertisements

On iOS, before any advertising identifier is used for tracking, the app
presents Apple's **App Tracking Transparency** prompt and asks for your
permission.

- If you **allow** tracking, Google may use your advertising identifier to show
  you personalised advertisements.
- If you **decline**, the app requests non-personalised advertisements. You will
  still see ads, but they will not be based on your advertising identifier.

You can change this choice at any time in **Settings → Privacy & Security →
Tracking** on iOS.

Google's handling of this data is governed by their own policies:

- Google Privacy Policy: https://policies.google.com/privacy
- How Google uses information from partner sites and apps:
  https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites

## Analytics

The app uses **Google Firebase Analytics** to understand how the game is used
in aggregate — for example how many players start a run, which themes are
chosen, and where players stop playing. This data is collected in a form that
does not identify you personally, and includes anonymous event names, an
app-instance identifier, device model, operating system version, and country.

We use this only to improve the game. Firebase Analytics is provided by Google
and is subject to the Google Privacy Policy linked above.

## Data we do not collect

We do not collect your name, email address, phone number, contacts, photos,
precise location, or any other personal information. The app has no sign-up,
no messaging, no user-generated content, and no social features.

## Children's privacy

Legend Run is not directed to children under 13. We do not knowingly collect
personal information from children under 13. If you believe a child has
provided personal information through the app, contact us at the address below
and we will address it.

## Sharing your information

We do not sell your data. We do not share your data with anyone other than the
service providers named above (Google AdMob and Google Firebase Analytics),
who process it on the terms of their own privacy policies.

## Your rights and choices

- **Advertising tracking:** iOS — Settings → Privacy & Security → Tracking.
  Android — Settings → Google → Ads.
- **Local data:** clear your scores from the leaderboard screen, or delete the
  app to remove all locally stored data.

## Changes to this policy

If this policy changes materially, we will update the "Last updated" date at
the top of this page and publish the revised version at the same address.

